  "authoredAt": "2026-11-10",
  "authoredFrom": "The CloudEvents HTTP protocol binding (binary content mode, header encoding) and NATS protocol binding 1.0.3-wip; full-event and min-event are the Go SDK's FullEvent and MinEvent (cloudevents/sdk-go v2/test/event_mocks.go) in canonical string form: Go writes exint 42 as \"42\", exbinary [0,1,2,3] as base64 \"AAECAw==\", times in RFC 3339 with trailing zeros trimmed, and SetData(\"text/json\", \"hello\") as the JSON string \"hello\".",
  "howToRead": {
    "encode": "Encoding `event` must give exactly `http` and `nats` (header names lower-case; `body` is the data as UTF-8 text). Decoding either must give `event` back.",
    "decode": "Decoding `headers` and `body` with `binding` must give `event`. These are messages other senders produce: Go's HTTP header canonicalisation, quoted strings, unnecessary percent-encoding.",
    "reject": "Decoding must fail.",
    "percent": "percentEncode(decoded) = encoded, and percentDecode(encoded) = decoded. `decodeOnly` entries need only decode."
  },
